  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 137 PM EDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nCurrently a few lingering showers across parts of the plateau and \nthe southern Appalachian Mountains early this afternoon. We should \ncontinue to see these slowly work their way through the region as \nthe trough also swings through overhead... No major impacts are \nexpected from these showers and few thunderstorms. \n\nMore notable is that it's turned much cooler today and even with the \nsun trying to come out it's going to feel like fall with \ntemperatures much lower than the previous weeks. This fall like \nweather will continue through the weekend with mostly clear skies \nand lower dew points. Rain chances don't look to return until at \nleast the middle of the week next week. A low and front look to try \nand move through the US, but models disagree with the timing and the \nstrength. But that's a problem for next week, in the meantime enjoy \nthe weather for the next several days.",
